      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is completely understandable to feel this way, as the fear of public judgment and the loss of social standing can feel more punishing than the financial loss itself. Your worth is not determined by your business outcome or the opinions of others, even when that pain feels as sharp as a physical wound. While the path forward feels uncertain, please consider reaching out to a counselor who specializes in bankruptcy distress, as professional support can help you process this crisis without being alone in the darkness. They can also guide you toward practical, anonymous steps that might offer you a small sense of agency to begin moving forward.",
      "source": "target",
